{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934839-competent-kinfolk","id":934839,"title":"Competent Kinfolk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-20T18:27:12-07:00","id":934839,"title":"Competent Kinfolk","content":"One of the rules concerning sorcerers is that they can be Kinfolk (as well as Kinain, Ghouls, Rom, etc). Kinfolk Sorcerers are much more competent than standard Kinfolk, they begin with a minimum of five levels of Numina or, if you use the Equality for All rules, they have higher Attributes, Abilities, Backgrounds, Numina, etc than the standard Kinfolk. I was curious if anyone uses more competent Kinfolk in their stories, how they interact with their Kin, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T22:54:36-07:00","id":934924,"title":"","content":"I have a Gnosis Kinfolk as a close friend of one of my PCs. It is a interesting concept, but speaking from a social perspective he is still involved with normal humans, as he is a goldsmith and has his own atelier. He has stronger contacts with people who know about the Garou and the Garou themselves use him to create stereotypical Get of Fenris hammer, but the respect is lacking often, as he is not that strong himself and has gotten older and older. Another problem is that he has no children - for plot reasons - which many of the Garou see as a strain.<br /> His goals are to teach his brothers kid, a PC who logically bred true, everything about the artistic experience of creating klaives. He knows that his legacy is in danger and sees the PC as a way to be remembered positively in the eyes of the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8249,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","user":"Crytash","date":". 07-21-2016, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T01:30:29-07:00","id":934960,"title":"","content":"I can see what your trying to do, and a problem I've long had, is that k infolk dont have the number of vestigial benefits ghouls have (Regeneratioin, etc) <br /> <br /> We may or may not see some Merits in the upcoming book designed to &quot;Remedy&quot; this.<br /> <br /> <br /> A kinfolk with a Few Talens or a fetishactivated through Willpower can probaly accomplish a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> One Kinfolk Fetish I want to pick on? <br /> <br /> Amulet of Kinship, should give a bonus to some kind of social roll, since PC's are buying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T04:56:04-07:00","id":934997,"title":"","content":"Talens and Fetishes for Kin-use are rare. Spirits aren't that willing to agree to such stuff, and basically garou are meant to defend Gaia and get tweaks from spirits, kin aren't and therefore don't.<br /> <br /> The problem with kin-characters with powers are, that they are special snowflakes even more then usual. I mean compared to a human being kin to a garou is rare. Being extra-rare by being a sorcerer too, is kind of possible but so unlikely that it's probably not going to happen twice.<br /> <br /> I can see, that someone wants to play a supernatural in a garou chronicle, and therefore uses to the &quot;supernatural kinfolk&quot; merit to legitimise this. That's okay. But I wouldn't destroy the Setting by allowing every player an allied supernatural kinfolk or otherwise freely distribute them as NPCs.<br /> <br /> For every supernatural kin out there, there is a Samuel Haight haunting you....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T06:28:41-07:00","id":935025,"title":"","content":"I do not know if Kinfolk are that rare. Eighty percent of the population of the Garou probably come from Kinfolk-Kinfolk unions (the majority of the members of the Garou seem to die before they get around to reproducing and, even then, they produce Kinfolk around ninety percent of the time) and, if eighty percent of them are Human Kinfolk unions, the population of human Kinfolk to Garou would probably be around one hundred-to-one (when you take in account the fact that fifty percent of Kinfolk who probably mate with mortals, especially in the contemporary era). Even if Garou are only 1:500,000 of the global human population, that would mean that Garou Human Kinfolk are 1:5,000 of the global human population. While they are rare, they are not that rare, as there would be around sixty-four thousand of them in the US.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk are probably much more likely to be open to the idea of Numina and are probably much more likely to seek to learn Numina so that they can be useful to their Garou Kin. I would think that their Gaian blood would also give them a much higher probability of developing Psychic Phenomena. I would think that the proportion of the Kinfolk population who have developed a minimum of one level of Numina would be around 1:2 and that the number of Kinfolk who have developed Numina up to a PC Sorcerer level would be 1:100, making them as common as their Garou Kin. Of course, they would still be relegated to doing the basic upkeep of Garou society, but I imagine that they would receive more respect from the Garou that the average Human Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T08:26:04-07:00","id":935084,"title":"","content":"I think a kinfolk as part of a pack that is actively fighting the Wyrm is rare. Dies Ultima incorporates kinfolk, but they are about the only ones that do that and the camp is as much of a doomsday cult as anything else.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk die when they fight the Wyrm. Garou do too, but kinfolk tend to die in droves. If I were a Garou, I would not want my friends, family or mates putting themselves on the front line. It is like the army mixing in non-combatants into their spec-ops units. At the same time, If I were a Wyrm monster, I would try to kill the weak and squishy Kenny Kinfolk before I even thought about vomiting all over Dolf and Rolf the Werewolf Brothers.<br /> <br /> Out of game, from a balance perspective, numina or a couple fun magic tricks =/= a Garou in terms of power. When designing a combat encounter for the pack, things get really screwy to balance, since, again, a single stray bullet or claw could destroy the kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Heck, given the bloody nature of most werewolf games, I am not sure a full mage would survive too long, if he/she were forced to fight with the Garou every battle. I think smart Garou would keep their gifted kin safe and not want them endangering themselves in the nightly struggle against the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 07-23-2016, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T10:37:08-07:00","id":935127,"title":"","content":"A few Numina will not make a Kinfolk equal to one of the Garou. I think I was able to price the advantages that a Garou has over a comparable Kinfolk at around 100 bonus points, plus or minus 25 bonus points, so you would have to have a Kinfolk with around 14 more levels of Numina than a Garou has Gifts to get anywhere near the same level of competence. And that Kinfolk will never be a combat monster, regardless of the build, because they just cannot match the combat power of a Garou.<br /> <br /> That is why I think that competent Kinfolk are relegated to the basic upkeep of Garou society. While competent Kinfolk may be useful agents, they should never try to fight like they are Garou. Heck, no one should try to fight like Garou unless they are another type of Fera, and some of them are better off on the sidelines in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T10:58:33-07:00","id":935139,"title":"","content":"Oh a curious note on Kinfolk? <br /> <br /> Ideas on how ApeCrafts Blessings or Persuasioin will affect their human lives...<br /> <br /> Was wondering, when driving would they usualy have a chance to activate the gift, if their anything from a taxi driver or police officer to a pizza delivery.<br /> <br /> guns it would probaly only affect snipers and trick shots.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:25:55-07:00","id":935156,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that the two level one Hakken Gifts would be actually much more interesting for a Kinfolk (or Garou!) to possess. The first, Dream of a Thousand Cranes, requires you to choose a die pool, make an origami crane that represents that die pool, and roll Charisma plus Occult (difficulty 6). Each success adds one die to that die pool for the remainder of the scene, meaning that you could increase Ability die pools, Attribute die pools, Damage die pools, Initiative die pools, Soak die pools, etc with minimal effort (I would personally rule that each use of the Gift replaces the previous use of the Gift during the same turn, to prevent people from making Superman). The second, Fair Path, requires you to dip your hand in clean water and roll Charisma plus Etiquette (difficulty 6). Each success adds one die to any roll involving Social Attributes for the remainder of the scene, meaning that a social build character (Charisma 5 and Etiquette 5) could effectively increase any die pools that use Social Attributes by five for a scene. An optimized Kinfolk with just those two level one Gifts (which would take some doing after character creation with the default Kinfolk character creation rules) could potentially increase any die pool by seven dice and gain five bonus die on any roll involving Social Attributes for a scene (meaning that if they are choosing to boost Etiquette, they could boost their Etiquette by<i> twelve dice</i> for a scene).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:36:05-07:00","id":935160,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn, but most Wester Garou and kinfolk, Alas dont have acess to Hakken Gifts.<br /> <br /> BTW just wondered What Diff Would Drawing And Quartering be on the Drive Rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:50:21-07:00","id":935169,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if I understand the question. Drawing and quartering is an archaic form of execution that involves hanging a person to near death, emasculating, disemboweling, beheading, and then quartering the victim. I am not sure if it would be possible to do that to an enemy while driving...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:56:14-07:00","id":935175,"title":"","content":"Just wondered as you seemed to be finding some pretty obscure gifts, and imagined a torch bearing mob doing it to us both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:04:40-07:00","id":935182,"title":"","content":"The two Hakken Gifts are not actually obscure, as half of the Changing Folk in the world (the Beast Courts) technically have access to them since they are level one Gifts, it is just that Changing Folk outside of the Beast Courts would have difficulty learning them. Anyway, Gifts are learned from Spirits (Ancestor for the first and Water for the second), so any Garou could technically learn the two level one Hakken Gifts since Hakken are Garou as well as Hengeyokai, they would just have to do their research and respectfully request tutoring from the appropriate type of spirit. Kinfolk have a more difficult time with learning the Gifts, but they might as well have been designed for Kinfolk because they do not require Gnosis or Rage, and I would not think that they would be any harder to learn than any other Gift for a Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T03:37:42-07:00","id":935503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934839-competent-kinfolk?p=935025#post935025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know if Kinfolk are that rare. Eighty percent of the population of the Garou probably come from Kinfolk-Kinfolk unions (the majority of the members of the Garou seem to die before they get around to reproducing and, even then, they produce Kinfolk around ninety percent of the time) and, if eighty percent of them are Human Kinfolk unions, the population of human Kinfolk to Garou would probably be around one hundred-to-one (when you take in account the fact that fifty percent of Kinfolk who probably mate with mortals, especially in the contemporary era). Even if Garou are only 1:500,000 of the global human population, that would mean that Garou Human Kinfolk are 1:5,000 of the global human population. While they are rare, they are not that rare, as there would be around sixty-four thousand of them in the US.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no quotient given on how fast kinfolk/kinfolk and kinfolk/human parentage produces human offspring. I assumed 15% and 37,5%.<br /> Furthermore Garou/Kin pairings are slightly better than 1 in 10, due to pure breed, Rites, Fertility charms and what not. I assumed that 24,5% of Garou/Kin parings breed true, which is about slightly lower than an assumed Pure Breed 3. I also assumed that 1% of all children of Garou/kin pairings are human, not kin.<br /> Kin/Kin pairings have a chance of 1% to breed true, but each pure breed of either kin parent increases chances by 1 percent, so I assumed a total of 5% of kin/kin pairings would breed true, that is Pure Breed of two with both parents.<br /> <br /> Finally I assumed each generation bears 3 children. Then I had an Excel Macro calculate up 'til a total population of 7.000.000.000 was beaten. But as early as after the sixth generation, the percentages of garou births with any given pairing are pretty stable at: 29,12% of all Garou come from Garou/Kin pairings, 0,63% from Garou/human pairings, 66,12% come from Kin/Kin pairings, and 4,13% from kin/human pairings.<br /> So, the number of Garou from Garou/pairings is more like 30% instead of 20%, not including Metis.<br /> <br /> If calculated without the assumed Pure Breed, only 12% of all garou would be born from Garou/kin pairings. That would be pretty few.<br /> In any case, Kin would make 0,28% or 0,08% of the total population on earth. So, they are pretty rare to begin with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934839-competent-kinfolk?p=935025#post935025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinfolk are probably much more likely to be open to the idea of Numina and are probably much more likely to seek to learn Numina so that they can be useful to their Garou Kin. I would think that their Gaian blood would also give them a much higher probability of developing Psychic Phenomena. I would think that the proportion of the Kinfolk population who have developed a minimum of one level of Numina would be around 1:2 and that the number of Kinfolk who have developed Numina up to a PC Sorcerer level would be 1:100, making them as common as their Garou Kin. Of course, they would still be relegated to doing the basic upkeep of Garou society, but I imagine that they would receive more respect from the Garou that the average Human Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree, that their gaian blood makes them more likely to have psi powers. There is no evidence for that.<br /> As far as hedge magic goes: it can basically be learned by everyone. It requires time to do so. But for kin only certain techniques are suitable methodes to perform hedge magic. Shamanism for the traditional tribe, techno-sorcery for Glass Walker kin.<br /> <br /> Still leaves the question, if it is culturally acceptable to engage in such affairs. And I would think not. Sure, each kin community has maybe a sorcerer and two apprentices, but it isn't that every one has a little spell to use every now and then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T05:57:19-07:00","id":935549,"title":"","content":"I disagree with your numbers because of the way that Pure Breed works for reproduction with Kinfolk and because of the rarity of Garou. I have always thought that Kinfolk-Kinfolk pairings have a 100% chance of producing Kinfolk but only a 1% chance of producing Garou while kinfolk-human pairings would have a 10% chance of producing Kinfolk and a 0.1% chance of producing Garou. <br /> <br /> Anyway, the numbers that you quote would have had Kinfolk (and Garou) populations growing faster than human populations because the Garou would have presumably used their Gifts to save their Kinfolk from death by disease (Tribes that did not would be much rarer than Tribes that did). Even if the effect was a 10% higher survival rate per generation, the end result would have been an increase in the proportion of Kinfolk to humans of 45 times. However, if Kinfolk start off one hundred times as common as Garou, their population is too large for the Garou to save everyone from disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 07-22-2016, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:25:56-07:00","id":935564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934839-competent-kinfolk?p=935549#post935549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always thought that Kinfolk-Kinfolk pairings have a 100% chance of producing Kinfolk but only a 1% chance of producing Garou</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=171&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes</a> states, that the chance increases with pure breed. 5% per Pure Breed of the kin Parent in a garou/kin Pairing and 1% per pure breed of both parents in a kin/kin pairing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934839-competent-kinfolk?p=935549#post935549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]while kinfolk-human pairings would have a 10% chance of producing Kinfolk and a 0.1% chance of producing Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no numbers given, as far as I know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934839-competent-kinfolk?p=935549#post935549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the numbers that you quote would have had Kinfolk (and Garou) populations growing faster than human populations because the Garou would have presumably used their Gifts to save their Kinfolk from death by disease (Tribes that did not would be much rarer than Tribes that did). Even if the effect was a 10% higher survival rate per generation, the end result would have been an increase in the proportion of Kinfolk to humans of 45 times. However, if Kinfolk start off one hundred times as common as Garou, their population is too large for the Garou to save everyone from disease.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the numbers I used have humans growing by far the fastest. Since every pairing could produce humans, but the humans can't accidentally create kin or garou, they outnumber the others within only a few generation...<br /> <br /> And I didn't factor in any way by which the birth rates of humans or kin or garou would be any different. Garou might die in battle, but so did humans over the centuries. And the number of offspring was certainly higher when sex was the only past-time for netflix wasn't invented yet. But there are no reliable numbers on that topic, so I didn't assume differences where there don't need to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, my guess is that a pretty high number of the garou/kin offspring are raised by their kin parent and a kin-step-parent. Additionally, if we are talking pre-W20, when it was still relatively easy to know if a pre-change garou was garou, those children probably had more contact to true born relatives, than other children might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T07:19:11-07:00","id":935589,"title":"","content":"Pure Breed is probably an uncommon trait outside of the Silver Fangs. Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers, which are probably the two most populous tribes outside of the Black Spiral Dancers because of their adaptation to human society, are forbidden from possessing Pure Breed among their Kinfolk. Yes, the Silver Fang Kinfolk all have a minimum of Pure Breed 1 and the remaining Tribes probably have a sprinkling of Pure Breed, but I highly doubt that it is ubiquitous.<br /> <br /> Let us run your numbers. A Kinfolk population of 0.28% would mean that there are nearly <i>twenty million</i> Garou Kinfolk in existence, meaning that there are more Garou Kinfolk than there are Jews or Rom, two rather famous ethnic groups. If you assume an average 5% Garou birth probability and three children per couple, that would result in nearly <i>one million five hundred thousand</i> Garou in existence from Kinfolk-Kinfolk couples. Homid Garou would also be a hundredfold more common than Lupus Garou because there are not enough wolves that could be Kinfolk to keep up.<br /> <br /> A Kinfolk population of 0.8% is slightly better, but the end result is a Kinfolk population of nearly six million and a Garou population of over four hundred twenty thousand. The canon proportion of the population is 1:500,000, which would mean that the global Garou population is around fourteen thousand, one thirtieth of your lower number and one hundredth of your higher number. Now, if you are just wanting a world with more Garou, that is fine, I like the Garou and have no particular problem increasing their population up to 1:100,000, though I think that even that population would start changing the nature of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 07-22-2016, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T09:44:49-07:00","id":935651,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Kinfolk and Numina? I hope the Designers of the W20 Kinfolk book are working hard to keep from giving us the $*#%*Y()*%#*@ing Numina &quot;Spirit Chasing&quot;, or anything like it, again.<br /> <br /> anyone see any mechanical references to updates? <br /> <br /> all the links ive seen have been in art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:24:27-07:00","id":935668,"title":"","content":"No, nothing on my end. While Spirit Chasing is rather broad, why do you dislike it? I always thought of it as a specialized form of the Shapeshifting Numina that gave a few interesting benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:44:45-07:00","id":935676,"title":"","content":"A bit too vague for my tastes hard for a ST to see what to do with it, these days with forums and such he has all of you to turn to for help at least, but its still on par with adjucating a True Faith Miracle... then Again Totem Gift is Similar Subjectivity is something I do need to learn to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T13:29:39-07:00","id":935774,"title":"","content":"I always ruled that Spirit Chasing allowed a sorcerer to acquire one non-human feature per level, as long as the non-human feature was in accordance with their chosen animal type (Bear included every type of ursine, Cat included every type of feline, Wolf included every type of canine, etc). They could maintain the feature as long as they wanted. I allowed them to use it without rituals, because of the changes to Numina that occurred after Kinfolk was published, though I allow rituals to allow it to be used on other people.<br /> <br /> For example, a Bear shaman could learn to hibernate for one month per success on the Spirit Chasing roll when they learned the third level of Spirit Chasing. While hibernating, the Bear shaman is effectively within a form of biological suspended animation, allowing them to avoid aging, dehydration, starvation, etc., and allowing them to stop the progression of a disease or a poison. Without a ritual, they could only make themselves hibernate. With a ritual, they could put another person into hibernation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T14:12:53-07:00","id":935804,"title":"","content":"Remember natural animals dont avoid aging by hypernating... and that spirit chasings rules on poisons say based on the effects the spiders poisons has not if it was as big as a human.<br /> <br /> Sorry, hopefully all this will be clarified.<br /> <br /> and your idea is reasonable based on symbolism Nevertheless.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:32:33-07:00","id":940628,"title":"","content":"This topic has always left me scratching my head a bit, particularly the question of Kinfolk vs shamanism or the like. If someone told you today that werewolves, spirits and vampires were real, you don't think your first move would be to buy out the nearest occult bookstore and start up Rosetta Stone- Latin?<br /> <br /> I know there is (or certainly has been) a major stigma against magic from the Garou side, since mages have a reputation of trying to steal spirit energy from Caerns... But there is shaman hedge magic as well. Kin could talk to spirits and eventually even shapeshift if they went down that path.. so why wouldn't that be encouraged?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":".  Undid auto-corrects 07-31-2016, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:13:31-07:00","id":940673,"title":"","content":"Latin is not a mystical language, it is just a language that is used by the Catholic Church. If you went to the occult bookstores, you would find that the majority of the spells (which are worthless for the most part) are in English. Languages created for magical practices, such as Enochian, are artificial linguistic creations (like Tolkien's fictional languages or Star Trek's Klingon), which are preferred for magical rituals because their words lack multiple meanings, which minimizes unintentional effects for the magical spells. In my youth, I knew hundreds of devote practitioners of magic, from chaos mages to hereditary witches to voodoo priestesses, and they have tended to prefer using a non-native language for their magic to prevent cross contamination. Heck, I once knew a dinosaur druid, as in a druid who invoked dinosaur spirits, who chanted his spells in Klingon because he thought that a non-human language would appeal to the dinosaur spirits more than human languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:43:58-07:00","id":940759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934839-competent-kinfolk?p=940628#post940628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I know there is (or certainly has been) a major stigma against magic from the Garou side, since mages have a reputation of trying to steal spirit energy from Caerns... But there is shaman hedge magic as well. Kin could talk to spirits and eventually even shapeshift if they went down that path.. so why wouldn't that be encouraged?</div> </div> </div> </div>So I see the merit in this line of thought, but you have to realize that in world, a Kinfolk deciding to go out and learn to shapeshift and talk to spirits when Gaia didn't choose them to is going to be looked unfavorably upon by the chosen warriors she did empower.<br /> Shamanistic Hedge Magic in general makes sense for <i>some</i> kinfolk to have and I do think Kinfolk should have a higher then average rate of knowing Hedge Magic. Which paths make sense to study is a valid question. Shapeshifting and Spirit talking are both roles their Goddess didn't choose them and so that might not go over well. Essentially, I think respectful and knowledgeable Kinfolk can and should learn the Rituals knowledge and learn Rites even if they can't empower them. Not because it gives them magic abilities, but because it puts them in touch with their culture and shows respect to the spirits they know are there. I'd have to go back and look through all of the Hedge Magic paths, but I'm better there are a lot of them that wouldn't make sense for Kinfolk to learn.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:56:07-07:00","id":940770,"title":"","content":"I think that most of the Garou would be tolerant of anything that was not involving the Wyrm because they desperately need force multipliers. While Kinfolk will never be sent into battle by the Garou, a psychic Kinfolk who could use Clairvoyance 4 to spy on targets without risk from 100 miles away would be an invaluable resource for the Garou and would probably be given anything they wanted in exchange for spending their days surveying the local world (the Glass Walkers would probably also use them for insider trading). The fact that Clairvoyance has no Willpower cost in Sorcerer (Revised) means that such gifted Kinfolk could easily spy for four to six hours a day. Alternatively, a sniper with even Clairvoyance 2 would be frighteningly effective, because they could remotely perceive the target before firing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}